LEAKYLEFT PUBLIC LICENSE
Version 0.0.0 — Too Late

THIS IS A FICTIONAL JOKE LICENSE AND A WORK OF SATIRE.
IT GRANTS NO PERMISSION TO PUBLISH OR USE REAL PERSONAL DATA.
NO LEGAL RIGHTS OR ENFORCEABLE OBLIGATIONS ARE CREATED.
NO LEGAL FORCE IS CLAIMED.

This is an original, independent parody using copyleft-style terminology. It is
not the GNU General Public License (GNU GPL), is not a version of it, and is not
affiliated with or endorsed by the GNU Project or the Free Software Foundation
(FSF). It is not a license for real software or personal data.

This document contains no real personal data. All people, data, permissions,
and duties in the scenario below are imaginary. Nothing here grants consent,
waives anyone's existing rights, or replaces anyone's existing duties.

PREAMBLE

You violated my privacy. Please don't violate my license too.

My personal information was never an open-source project. You appear to have
forked it anyway.

If you insist on copying, spreading, modifying, or exploiting my personal
information without asking, please treat every copy and remix as if it came
with copyleft terms. Carry the notice. Explain the changes. Pass the terms on.
Then imagine applying exactly the same arrangement to yourself.

If that last part makes you uncomfortable, the preamble is working.

The following provisions apply only inside this fiction. Their apparent grant
of permission is part of the joke: no permission was ever granted.

0. DEFINITIONS

"I," "my," and "Source Person" refer to the imaginary person whose private life
someone mistook for a public repository.

"You" means the fictional copier, redistributor, processor, or other person
who decided that asking was an optional dependency.

"Covered Fiction" means the wholly imaginary personal information discussed
in this satire. No actual records are supplied here, and no real person's
information is covered by this document.

"Copy" includes a fictional download, screenshot, export, backup, mirror, or
forward. Changing the file extension does not change the plot.

1. REDISTRIBUTION

Every copy of the Covered Fiction must carry this notice and these fictional
terms, including every forwarded, uploaded, mirrored, sold, or otherwise
redistributed copy. Each downstream recipient inherits the same terms.

"I only sent it to one person" is distribution with an optimistic growth
forecast. Calling the copy a backup does not make it my idea.

Removing the notice does not remove the fictional conditions. It merely adds
another deletion to the list of things you chose to do instead of asking me.

2. DERIVATIVE WORKS

For this joke, Derivative Works include aggregation, enrichment, matching or
joining datasets, profiling, inferred attributes, and other processing of the
Covered Fiction. AI training and models trained on it are included too.

Every such derivative inherits this notice and the same fictional terms, as
do its subsequent copies and derivatives. A new column is not a new consent
receipt. A confidence score is not permission with decimal places.

"It is only a model now" is not a clean-room implementation of my private life.
Renaming the dataset "insights" does not make it your autobiography.

3. CORRESPONDING SOURCE

With every redistribution or Derivative Work, provide the complete fictional
acquisition and processing history: where the information was obtained, how
it reached you, each intermediary, every transformation and dataset join,
the methods used to produce inferences or train models, and who received the
result. Pass this history on with the notice and terms.

"Found it online" is not a provenance trail. "Proprietary methodology" is not
an acceptable explanation for how my weekend became your prediction engine.

Provide the recipe, not another serving of my private life. Corresponding
Source means an imaginary audit trail here, never a requirement or permission
to publish more real personal data.

4. SHAREALIKE

If you treat my information as available for copying, redistribution,
aggregation, profiling, AI training, or other misuse, imagine your equivalent
information receiving exactly the same treatment under these same terms.

No "my privacy is different" exception is available. Neither is a proprietary
edition in which only the person holding the spreadsheet gets boundaries.

If you would like to opt out of this imaginary reciprocity, congratulations:
you have discovered why I wanted to be asked before any of this started.

This mirror is the joke. It is not a request or permission to expose your
information, retaliate, or invade anyone else's privacy. Nobody's real data
becomes fair game.

5. TERMINATION

Any permission you think this document grants terminates immediately upon
the discovery that it never granted any. Effective date: before your first
unauthorized copy.

There is nothing to reinstate. A completed checklist of the other fictional
clauses cannot manufacture the consent that was missing at the beginning.

Backward compatibility is guaranteed: you did not have permission under any
previous version either. Please stop treating the absence of consent as a
feature flag.

6. REAL-WORLD EFFECT: NONE

These fictional terms grant no permission to collect, copy, publish, disclose,
redistribute, process, train on, or otherwise use real personal information.
They create no legal rights, remedies, or enforceable obligations. Existing
rights and duties are unaffected. Reading, attaching, redistributing, or
pretending to comply with this document does not change that.

This document is not legal advice. It supplies no consent receipt, deletion
mechanism, recall function, or working time machine. Attaching a LICENSE file
cannot retroactively make an unauthorized copy authorized.

END OF FICTIONAL TERMS

Copy left. Consent still missing.
